-- title:
--   First Drinfeld section is the origin at the Gauss place
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\kappa_A$ denotes the residue field of a valuation subring $A$, and for an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ the symbol $A_0$ denotes the valuation subring $A.\mathrm{comap}\,(\mathrm{algebraMap}\ k_0\ \overline{\mathbb Q})$ of $k_0$.
--
--   **Base data.** Fixed are: a prime $q$ with $5 \le q$; a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$; a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ satisfying `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ lies in `A.nonunits`; a finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC` $\kappa_A\ M'$ — the intermediate field of `LaurentSeries` $\kappa_A$ generated over $\kappa_A$ by `jqModC` $\kappa_A$ and `jqNModC` $\kappa_A\ M'$ — together with `hW`, which says that $W$ consists exactly of the members of `ssPlaces` $q\ M'\ \kappa_A$, the places satisfying the predicate `IsSupersingularPlace` $q\ M'$ (a place here being a valuation subring of the ambient field which contains the image of the base field, is not the whole field, and is a principal ideal ring). Further, `hle` asserts the inclusion `modularFunctionFieldBar` $M'$ $\le$ `fieldBar` $q\ M'$ of intermediate fields of `LaurentSeries` $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$: on the left the field generated by the coefficientwise images of the full level-$M'$ modular function field, on the right `xHFunctionFieldBar` $(q^2M')$ `(levelH` $q\ M')$, where `levelH` $q\ M'$ is the kernel of the reduction map $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, that is, the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$. Next, $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of `modularFunctionFieldBar` $M'$ relative to $A$ with values in `modularFunctionFieldC` $\kappa_A\ M'$: a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of the source, a surjective residue homomorphism onto the target with kernel the maximal ideal, a map on places preserving degrees, compatibility of membership and of residues with $A$ on constants, the existence for every nonzero $f$ of a scalar making $f$ integral with nonzero residue, and compatibility of divisors with orders under the map on places. The hypothesis `hR₀` requires that for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in `LaurentSeries` $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar` $M'$, that image lies in `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa_A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Finally $s$ is an element of $W$.
--
--   **Small constants.** Fixed are an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and an element $\pi_0$ of $k_0$ lying in $A$ (`hπ`), subject to: `hdvr`, $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring; `hunif`, the maximal ideal of $A_0$ is generated by $\pi_0$; `hhens`, $A_0$ is a Henselian local ring; `hres`, the residue field of $A_0$ is algebraically closed; and `hκ`, every $a \in A$ admits $c \in k_0$ with $c \in A$ and $a - c$ in the maximal ideal of $A$.
--
--   **Auxiliary prime and function field.** Fixed are a prime $\ell'$ with $\ell' \ne q$, $3 \le \ell'$ and $\ell' \nmid M'$; an element $\xi$ of $k_0$ which is a primitive $(q\ell')$-th root of unity (`hξ`), together with `hιξ`, the existence of a ring homomorphism $k_0 \to \mathbb C$ carrying $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell'))$; an intermediate field $K$ of `LaurentSeries` $k_0$ over $k_0$ with `hK`: $K$ is `laurentBaseChange` $k_0$ of `xHFunctionField` $((q\ell')^2M')$ `(levelH` $(q\ell')\ M')$, i.e. the subfield generated over $k_0$ by the coefficientwise images of the function field of the $X_H$ of level $(q\ell')^2M'$ with $H$ the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell'$; an algebra structure of $A_0$ on $K$ compatible with the tower $A_0 \subseteq k_0 \subseteq K$; and a nonzero element $j$ of $K$ whose Laurent expansion over $k_0$ is the coefficientwise image of `jq`, the $\mathsf q$-expansion $\mathsf q^{-1}\cdot$`jNumQ` of the modular $j$-invariant (`hj`).
--
--   **Structural hypotheses for the rigid datum.** The hypothesis `hℓ` states that for every commutative ring $T$ that is an $A_0$-algebra, every Weierstrass curve $W$ over $T$, every variable change $C$ and every `LevelPData` $D$ over $T$, if `IsLevelPStructure W ℓ' D` holds (the two points satisfy the affine equation, their $x$-coordinates are roots of $W$'s $\ell'$-th pre-$\Psi$ polynomial, and the two independence elements are units) then `IsLevelPStructure (C • W) ℓ' (D.variableChange C)` holds. The hypothesis `hM` states the corresponding equivariance of `IsGamma0PowAt` under variable change, with the transported polynomial `kernelVariableChangeDeg C (gamma0PowDeg p k) h`. Further, $\mathcal G$ is a family of relative group laws `GroupLaws` $A_0$ on projective Weierstrass models with unit discriminant over $A_0$-algebras, with `h𝒢` asserting that each is a chord–tangent law (given by a points evaluation) and `h𝒢O` asserting that each identity section factors through the origin chart by a ring homomorphism killing $x/y$ and $z/y$; $\mathcal T$ is a `LevelTransport` $A_0\ \mathcal G\ q$, i.e. a functorial transport of raw Drinfeld pairs along $A_0$-algebra maps and variable changes preserving the level condition, with `h𝒯` asserting that this transport is compatible with the two sections under the induced maps of projective models. The hypotheses `hVC` and `hCO` assert, for every $A_0$-algebra $T$ (respectively every $A_0$-algebra map $f : T \to T'$) and every projective Weierstrass curve, the existence of a graded ring homomorphism of the graded projective-model rings, with the irrelevant ideal of the target contained in the image of that of the source, satisfying `IsVariableChangeHom` (respectively `IsCoefficientHom`). Together with $\ell'$, $M'$, $q$ these data produce the rigid Weierstrass datum $\mathcal R :=$ `rigidDataPow` $A_0\ \ell'\ M'\ q\$`hℓ hM` $\mathcal G\ \mathcal T$, whose level object has three components: a $\Gamma_0$-power component at the prime factors of $M'$, a level-$\ell'$ `LevelPData` component, and a Drinfeld pair at $q$.
--
--   **The Tate point and its chart.** Fixed are: $P_0$, a `LevelModuliPackageAbs` for $\mathcal R$'s associated level moduli datum, consisting of an $A_0$-algebra $B_0$ with a universal point `P₀.univ` such that every point over an $A_0$-algebra is the image of the universal one under a unique $A_0$-algebra map; a point $x_0$ of the datum over $K$ whose $j$-invariant, read in `LaurentSeries` $k_0$, is `jqNModC` $k_0\ (q\ell')$ (`hx₀`); an $A_0$-algebra map `clC` from $B_0$ to the chart algebra `chartAlgFin` $A_0\ K\ j$ (the $A_0$-subalgebra `chartAlg` $A_0\ K\ \{j\}$ of $K$) with `hclC`: the image in $K$ of `clC b` is `P₀.classify x₀ b` for every $b$.
--
--   The hypothesis `hμ` pins $x_0$ down as the Tate point: there exist a variable change $C$ over `LaurentSeries` $k_0$ and a raw datum $r$ of $\mathcal R$ over $K$ such that (a) the class of $r$ is $x_0$; (b) writing $(x_{\mathrm c}, y_{\mathrm c})$ for `cuspPoint` $k_0\ (q\ell')$ at the unit determined by $\xi$ and the vector $(1,0)$, one has $C.u\,(2x_{\mathrm c} + 1/6) = 2y_{\mathrm c} + x_{\mathrm c}$, $C.r = -1/12$, $C.s = -1/2$, $C.t = 1/24$ (the last three as constant Hahn series); (c) the curve of $r$, base-changed to `LaurentSeries` $k_0$, equals $C \bullet$ `tateBase` $k_0\ (q\ell')$; (d) for every prime factor $p$ of $M'$, every field $F'$, every ring homomorphism $f : k_0 \to F'$ and every primitive $p^{v_p(M')}$-th root of unity $\zeta$ in $F'$, the $\Gamma_0$-component polynomial `r.level.1 p`, pushed to `LaurentSeries` $F'$, equals `kernelVariableChangeDeg` of $C$ pushed along $f$, in degree `gamma0PowDeg` $p\ v_p(M')$, applied to $\prod_{a} (X - (\mathrm{toricPoint}\ F'\ (q\ell')\ \zeta^a)_1)$, the product over $a \in [1, p^{v_p(M')}/2]$ with $p \nmid a$; (e) the level-$\ell'$ component `r.level.2.1`, pushed to `LaurentSeries` $k_0$, equals the $C$-variable change of `cuspData` $k_0\ (q\ell')$ at the unit determined by $\xi$ and the vectors $(q,0)$, $(0,-q)$ in $(\mathbb Z/q\ell')^2$; and (f) there exist $P_x, P_y, Q_x, Q_y$ in $K$ whose Laurent expansions are the four coordinates `xP`, `yP`, `xQ`, `yQ` of the $C$-variable change of `cuspData` $k_0\ (q\ell')$ at the vectors $(\ell',0)$, $(0,-\ell')$, and such that `IsSectionThrough r.level.2.2.P` $P_x\ P_y$ and `IsSectionThrough r.level.2.2.Q` $Q_x\ Q_y$ hold, i.e. each of the two Drinfeld sections at $q$ is cut out in the $z$-chart with these affine coordinates.
--
--   Finally $\theta$ is a ring homomorphism from the residue field of $A_0$ to $\kappa_A$ with `hθ`: $\theta$ carries the residue of $a \in A_0$ to the residue in $A$ of the image of $a$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Under these hypotheses the following holds. Let $\Omega$ be a field which is an algebra over $\kappa_A$, let $V$ be a place of $\Omega$ over $\kappa_A$ with valuation ring $\mathcal O_V$, and let $\rho$ be a ring homomorphism from `chartAlgFin` $A_0\ K\ j$ to $\mathcal O_V$. Let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of $K$ satisfying `hW₀`: an element $f$ of $K$ belongs to $W_0$ if and only if there are power series $x, y$ over $A_0$ with the reduction of $y$ modulo the maximal ideal of $A_0$ nonzero and $f \cdot y = x$ in `LaurentSeries` $k_0$, the two power series being pushed to $k_0$ and viewed as Hahn series (the Gauss valuation ring). Assume `hker`: for every $h$ in the chart algebra, $\rho(h)$ vanishes in $\Omega$ if and only if the image of $h$ in $K$ lies in `W₀.nonunits`. Then, for every $A_0$-algebra structure on $\mathcal O_V$, every $A_0$-algebra homomorphism $\rho_A : B_0 \to \mathcal O_V$ with $\rho_A b = \rho(\mathrm{clC}\ b)$ for all $b$ (`hρA`), and every raw datum $x_V$ of $\mathcal R$ over $\mathcal O_V$ whose class in the points of $\mathcal R$ over $\mathcal O_V$ is the image of `P₀.univ` under the map induced by $\rho_A$ (`hxV`), there exists a ring homomorphism
--   $$\chi_P : \mathrm{OriginChartRing}\,(x_V.\mathrm{level}.2.2.\mathrm{curve}) \to \Omega$$
--   — the source being the degree-zero part of the localisation of the graded projective-model ring of the Drinfeld-pair curve at the coordinate $y$ — such that the three following assertions hold: first, the morphism $\operatorname{Spec}\Omega \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O_V$ induced by the structure map $\mathcal O_V \to \Omega$, followed by the underlying scheme morphism of the first Drinfeld section $x_V.\mathrm{level}.2.2.P$, equals the morphism induced by $\chi_P$ followed by `originChartι` of that curve; second, $\chi_P(\mathrm{xOverY}) = 0$; third, $\chi_P(\mathrm{zOverY}) = 0$.
--
--   At the generic point of the Gauss branch of the two-chart integral model attached to $j$, the first section of the Drinfeld level-$q$ structure carried by the universal object specialises to the origin of the projective Weierstrass model: the section factors through the chart where $y$ is invertible, with $x/y$ and $z/y$ both zero. The hypothesis `hμ` identifies the point over $K$ with the Tate curve of level $q\ell'M'$ together with its cusp level data, so the assertion is the statement that the $\mu_q$-part of the Tate torsion reduces to the identity on the Gauss branch. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_place_ringHom_chartAlgFin_residue_eq_originChart_levelAut_of_forall_nsmul_eq_zero_of_tatePoint`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_place_ringHom_chartAlgFin_residue_eq_originChart_levelAut_of_forall_nsmul_eq_zero_of_tatePoint) in the analysis of the reduction of the modular curve $X_H$ at $q$.
